tt.95.210503"}], "earliest_date": "2005-11-16", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Martinis:2005lcs"], "abstracts": [{"source": "APS", "value": "Dielectric loss from two-level states is shown to be a dominant decoherence source in superconducting quantum bits. Depending on the qubit design, dielectric loss from insulating materials or the tunnel junction can lead to short coherence times. We show that a variety of microwave and qubit measurements are well modeled by loss from resonant absorption of two-level defects. Our results demonstrate that this loss can be significantly reduced by using better dielectrics and fabricating junctions of small area $\\ensuremath{\\lesssim}10\\text{ }\\text{ }\\ensuremath{\\mu}{\\mathrm{m}}^{2}$. With a redesigned phase qubit employing low-loss dielectrics, the energy relaxation rate has been improved by a factor of 20, opening up the possibility of multiqubit gates and algorithms.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "APS"}}], "refereed": true, "titles": [{"source": "APS", "title": "Decoherence in Josephson Qubits from Dielectric Loss"}], "facet_author_name": ["1914865_Kristopher Cooper", "1961223_Robert F. McDermott", "1955071_Sangwon Oh", "1929794_K. Cicak", "1929801_R.W. Simmonds", "1933164_John M. Martinis", "1991649_C. Yu", "2027667_M. Steffen", "2034320_Georgios P.D. Pappas", "2113033_Markus Ansmann", "1458806_Joseph D. Osborn"], "core": true, "imprints": [{"date": "2005-11-16"}], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:2730858", "updated": "2025-06-16T19:07:16.614013"}, "curated": true, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys.Rev.Lett.", "Phys. Rev. Lett."]}}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.95.210503&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.95.210503&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.95.210503&size=5&p